{"author":{"id":"7674679dac9170669f752d932f8b5955b1d55717359e13b1c1e687003c7bb99f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789867472,"nonce":"XOZpcbzxOmWNuJsv2idAc8QEUXw=","title":"Task: Implement the iteration entity (namespace, ops, subcache, resolver)","message":"aba17f4 decides the shape; this builds it. See doc/design/configurable-schema.md D5.\n\nA new entity on the same dag machinery as issues: namespace refs/iterations, ops Create / SetDates / SetCapacity / SetState, a snapshot, an excerpt, a SubCache and a resolver so issues can reference it. Issues point at it through a cardinality-1 relation of kind `iteration`; Jira sprints and Linear cycles both map onto it.\n\nNon-atomic by construction, so the ordering matters: create the next iteration, move the unfinished issues, THEN close the old one. A crash mid-way then leaves 'some issues already moved to the next sprint', which reads correctly and is idempotent to retry. Closing first would strand issues in a closed iteration.\n\nSized at roughly a third of story 6555e36 — it was missing from the task list, which is why it is here.","files":null}]}